{"tool_name":"newick_utilities","contents":["galaxy","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"newick_utilities","home":"https://www.ezlab.org/","summary":"The Newick Utilities are a set of command-line tools for processing phylogenetic trees. They can process arbitrarily large amounts of data and do not require user interaction, which makes them suitable for automating phylogeny processing tasks.","addition_date":"2017-12-06T18:14:44Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:34:29.575739Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["Newick Utilities"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:newick_utilities","credit":[{"email":"thomas.junier@unine.ch","name":"Thomas Junier","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/tjunier/newick_utils"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-CZ","cornelius.roemer"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Phylogenetic tree analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0324"},{"term":"Phylogenetic tree generation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0323"},{"term":"Phylogenetic tree reconstruction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3478"}]}],"name":"Newick Utilities","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btq243","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: We present a suite of UNIX shell programs for processing any number of phylogenetic trees of any size. They perform frequently-used tree operations without requiring user interaction. They also allow tree drawing as scalable vector graphics (SVG), suitable for high-quality presentations and further editing, and as ASCII graphics for command-line inspection. As an example we include an implementation of bootscanning, a procedure for finding recombination breakpoints in viral genomes. Availability: C source code, Python bindings and executables for various platforms are available from http://cegg.unige.ch/newick_utils. The distr